+// <n>-<size> holds the process's nth repack buffer. A finished file is mapped read-only and its
+// tensors aren't repacked again. The first process to find none writes <name>.partial under an
+// exclusive lock, and ggml_backend_cpu_repack_file_commit(), once the model has loaded, renames it
+// into place; a process that finds another writing uses an unlinked file. The key must change
+// whenever the repacked bytes would: the caller makes it from the model file and this CPU module.
